body.p:
[0003] In air vehicles, wing structures are used to create the lifting force required by the vehicle at the relevant flight speed. It is preferred that the wing area is higher so that the vehicle can produce the desired lifting force without losing grip at low speeds. However, at highSVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1130.087speeds, large wing areas are not preferred because they cause high drag. For this reason, telescopic wings are used to increase the lifting force at tow speeds and to reduce wing drag at high speeds.
